    "rawMarkdown": "Labels from the reports cap at around 0.9. To get past that the biggest improvements for me came from:\n a) ensembles of models\n b) data augmentation (flipping, zoom, etc).\n\nIf you check the code section there are many posts about how to get to the 0.943 score that is so common on the leaderboard, you could start by checking what they did.\n\nHope it helps you. Regards",
    "content": "<p>Labels from the reports cap at around 0.9. To get past that the biggest improvements for me came from:\n a) ensembles of models\n b) data augmentation (flipping, zoom, etc).</p>\n<p>If you check the code section there are many posts about how to get to the 0.943 score that is so common on the leaderboard, you could start by checking what they did.</p>\n<p>Hope it helps you. Regards</p>",
